  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_LeastPrivilege  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_LeastPrivilege.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows the model to assign Permitted outcome to operations where the caller's role is not allowed to perform the operation, directly violating least privilege.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_CareTeamAuthorization  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_CareTeamAuthorization.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows RecordsLookup operations to succeed for clinicians not on the patient's care team, violating the core ownership-based access control rule.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess, FR_006_CareTeamMembershipGating
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_006_CareTeamMembershipGating: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditCompleteness  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_AuditCompleteness.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows operations to exist with audit entries that do not correctly attribute the operation to the actual caller or patient, breaking auditability.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_008_AlwaysOnAudit, AttributionCorrectness
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_008_AlwaysOnAudit: FAIL (expected)
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_PermissionMatrix  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_PermissionMatrix.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows the permission matrix to be redefined with incorrect role-operation assignments, such as granting AuditOfficer access to RecordsLookup or Doctor access to AuditSearch.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, PermissionGrounding
      - LeastPrivilege: PASS (vacuous?)
      - PermissionGrounding: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_IGRoleRestriction  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_IGRoleRestriction.als
    rationale: Removing this fact allows clinical roles (doctor, nurse, etc.) to perform AuditSearch operations, leaking audit data to non-IG users and violating role-based authorization.
    expected to FAIL: FR_011_IGAuditAccess
      - FR_011_IGAuditAccess: FAIL (expected)

